RECOVERABLE SLICE  —  TRIPLE FORM
→ 005.1 → Programming Theory / Data Structures

TYPES
  Slice         constrained view / mock form / grounded invariant surface
                lower-dimensional projection of a larger geometry
  Declaration   explicit operators that generate the slice
                (no hidden assumptions; start from zero)
  History       recorded path from ambient geometry to the slice
                (how the constraints were applied)
  Triple        (Slice, Declaration, History)
  Tuple         Slice alone
  Ambient       full relational operator geometry
                (Niemeier-like lattice / unreduced flux system)
  Lift          inverse reconstruction
                (triadic re-lifting / Maass-style completion)

FUNDAMENTALS
  A slice is generated, not primitive.
  You declare the operators that produce the slice you need.
  Reconstructability requires all three components together.
  Declaration + History supply the missing coordinates of the Triple.
  The Triple is a lossless embedding:
    the Slice stays usable in its own theory-class
    the other two components guarantee an inverse lift.

LOSS CONDITION
  Store only the Tuple  →  pre-image is under-determined
  Reconstruction map becomes many-to-one
  Original structure cannot be recovered
  Information is irreversibly lost

PRESERVATION RULE
  Keep data as declared Triple.
  Slice remains a valid local view.
  Lift can restore full geometry when required.

ANALOGY
  Mock form          = Slice
  Niemeier lattice   = Ambient geometry
  Maass completion   = upward repair / Lift
  McKay-Thompson T_g = Slice detached from VOA + Monster action
                       (function alone does not recover the module)
